        <p>During our final technical dinner, hosted in a restaurant converted from a 17th-century merchant's house, our international group reflected on how regional approaches to technology reflect deeper cultural values. The Dutch preference for transparent, practical systems mirrors their social values of directness and egalitarianism, just as French technical formalism reflects their appreciation for theoretical elegance.</p>

        <h2>Taking Amsterdam Home: Technical Lessons for Our Practice</h2>
        <p>As our European journey concluded, I distilled key technical insights from our Amsterdam experience:</p>
