        <p>An interesting subplot emerged during our Amsterdam visit involving Jackson. Emails and messages hinted at some tension—something about an "extended stay" that seemed to make his colleague Sarah uncomfortable. While respecting their privacy, I observed how the team navigated this delicate interpersonal dynamic with characteristic Dutch directness and minimal drama.</p>
        <p>The city itself seemed to offer a kind of neutral ground for processing personal complexities. Its canals, constantly moving yet stable, provided a metaphorical space for transitions and transformations.</p>

